    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d696">

                <pb facs="0694" n="624" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg624"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.20/72</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of War</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dern</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-04-09">April 9, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Your letter of March 22,
                        1934,<anchor n="85" xml:id="d696-f1"/> enclosing a draft of a proposed
                    contract between the United States of America and Brazil for the services of two
                    Army officers, is acknowledged.</p>
                <p>The contract has been carefully studied and a re-draft is enclosed.<anchor n="86"
                        xml:id="d696-f2"/> One major change is included, i. e., to make the term of
                    the contract uniform throughout the document. This was not the case in the
                    Brazilian draft.</p>
                <p>The enclosed re-draft includes the original wording of the Brazilian draft as
                    well as the proposed changes and additions, the words replaced or omitted are
                    lined out as follows—<del rendition="#strikethrough">words</del>—the
                    substitutions or additions are underlined as—<hi rendition="#underline"
                        >letters</hi>. It is the opinion of the War Department that the changes made
                    in the contract should be approved.</p>
                <p>The officers who will compose the mission are: <list>
                        <item>Lieut. Colonel Rodney H. Smith, C.A.C.</item>
                        <item>Captain William D. Hohenthal, C.A.C.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>It appears to be the desire of the Brazilian Government that the mission arrive
                    in Brazil as soon as practicable. To that end it is <pb facs="0695" n="625"
                        xml:id="pg625"/> requested that every effort be made to secure prompt
                    signature of the contract as amended.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. H. Dern</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
